/* =============================================================================
 * sec-about.css — VIEWPORT RETUNE for the #about band ("STATEMENT & RAIL")
 * -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Target: 818px (900px viewport minus the 82px sticky header that floats over
 * every band). Measured before: 993px @1440x900, 884px @1024x900.
 *
 * WHAT OWNS THIS BAND: structural.css block [AN] (6519-6692) plus its own
 * one-row sub-block [AN-b] (6694-6750). Those are the LAST #about rules in the
 * file (verified: no `#about` / `.ab-` / `doc-list` selector exists past 6750),
 * so [AN]/[AN-b] are what this sheet has to beat. Every selector below MATCHES
 * the winning selector's specificity exactly and wins on source order only —
 * this sheet is linked after structural.css.
 *
 * WHAT IS NOT TOUCHED — the band is owner-approved and the copy is frozen:
 *   - no font-size anywhere (the 50px h2, the 40px manifesto, the 13.5/13px
 *     deks all keep their shipped scale). Height is bought with padding, gaps
 *     and box geometry, never by shrinking type.
 *   - no line-height, no max-width/measure, no colour, no DOM, no row counts.
 *   - the plate assignment (1400 -> large, 1200x1594 -> upper, 512 -> compact
 *     square) is left exactly as [AN] set it, because that assignment is what
 *     earns the band its retina numbers.
 *
 * GATING: everything except the band padding sits inside `min-width: 981px`,
 * the same gate [AN-a]/[AN-b] use and for the same documented reason — below
 * 981 the layout is the stacked one and structural re-declares .ab-cluster,
 * .ab-links and .doc-list__item inside `max-width: 980/860/560` blocks. A
 * base-level override here would out-rank those media blocks on source order
 * (media queries add no specificity) and silently break the tablet and phone
 * layouts. Gating by min-width leaves them untouched, with no reset to get
 * wrong. The one exception is the band padding: [AN] declares it exactly once,
 * at base, with no media re-declaration, so overriding it at base is safe and
 * keeps the rhythm continuous through the 980 boundary.
 * ========================================================================== */


/* ---- 1. BAND RHYTHM ------------------------------------------------------
 * [AN]:6557 sets `padding-block: clamp(56px, 6.6vw, 96px)` -> 95/95 @1440.
 * That predates the global token being retuned to `--ds-section-py:
 * clamp(48px, 5vw, 76px)` (tokens.css:118 -> 72/72 @1440), which left #about
 * as the ONLY band on the page padded 23px MORE generously than the site
 * rhythm. This brings it back inside that rhythm rather than outside it:
 * 58/58 @1440 and 48/48 @1024, and the 48px floor is the global token's own
 * floor, so the phone band never goes tighter than the site standard.
 * Specificity (1,1,0) — identical to [AN]:6557, so source order decides. */
#about.section { padding-block: clamp(48px, 4.1vw, 58px); }


@media (min-width: 981px) {

  /* ---- 2. THE RAIL -------------------------------------------------------
   * The single biggest consumer. [AN] pins the rail at
   * `height: clamp(360px, 28vw, 420px)` -> 403px @1440, 360px @1024 (its
   * floor), and .ab-split is `align-items: stretch`, so the statement panel is
   * dragged to that height too. The copy's own content only measures 254px
   * @1440 / 225px @1024 — the rail was carrying ~150px of pure air on the copy
   * side. Shortening the rail costs the copy nothing at all.
   *
   * RETINA IS NOT HARMED — IT IMPROVES. [AN] reports worst-image retina 1.45x
   * @1440, retina being min(naturalW/boxW, naturalH/boxH)/2. On the tall plate
   * HEIGHT is the binding axis (1400/403 = 3.47 < 1400/308 = 4.55), so a
   * shorter box makes it sharper, and the weak 512x512 source is pinned to the
   * col-2/row-2 measure, which this rule shrinks in step. Measured after:
   *   @1440  512-square 1.43x -> 1.71x   tall plate 1.74x -> 2.06x
   *   @1024  512-square 1.71x -> 2.00x   tall plate 1.94x -> 2.36x
   *
   * The compact measure is shrunk WITH the height on purpose. Cutting height
   * alone would leave row 2 (the 512 square) taller than row 1, inverting the
   * rail's hierarchy so the weakest source got the biggest right-hand cell.
   * Held at ~1:1.18 (upper cell taller than the foot square) exactly as
   * shipped: @1440 152 wide / 173 upper; @1024 128 wide / 158 upper. */
  #about .ab-cluster {
    height: clamp(296px, 23.2vw, 336px);
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) clamp(128px, 10.2vw, 152px);
    grid-template-rows:    minmax(0, 1fr) clamp(128px, 10.2vw, 152px);
  }

  /* ---- 3. THE MANIFESTO / CARDS ROW --------------------------------------
   * Both items keep the SAME margin-top as each other — [AN-b] centres this
   * row (`#about .container { align-items: center }`), so an unequal pair
   * would shift the sentence off the card stack's optical centre. 44 -> 36
   * @1440. */
  #about .ab-manifesto      { margin-top: clamp(26px, 2.5vw, 36px); }
  #about .doc-list.ab-links { margin-top: clamp(26px, 2.5vw, 36px); }

  /* Card stack: [AN-b] gives each card 15px block padding around 49px of
   * content (title + one-line dek) in a 596px-wide row — an 81px box for 49px
   * of type. 12px still clears the type comfortably (75px box, well over the
   * 44px tap-target floor) and reads as the compact index row it is, not as a
   * squashed card. The inter-card gap comes off with it so the stack stays
   * proportionate rather than turning into three cards with a moat. */
  #about .doc-list.ab-links { gap: clamp(8px, 0.7vw, 10px); }
  #about .doc-list__item    { padding: 12px 18px; }

  /* ---- 4. THE CTA ROW ----------------------------------------------------
   * 37 -> 32 @1440. The buttons themselves are untouched. */
  #about .ab-cta { margin-top: clamp(24px, 2.2vw, 32px); }
}

/* NOTE ON THE TWO SITE-WIDE TRAPS
 * 1. .ab-cluster and .doc-list.ab-links are both .wow-stagger containers. This
 *    sheet sets NO `opacity` on them or on any of their direct children
 *    (figures / .doc-list__item), so nothing can be frozen invisible.
 * 2. .ab-cluster figure is `overflow: hidden`. Its only content is an
 *    object-fit:cover <img> at width/height 100%, so a shorter box re-crops
 *    the photo, it cannot clip a text run. Verified empirically after every
 *    change: scrollHeight <= clientHeight on every descendant of #about, and
 *    all 15 text runs still present. See the report.
 */


