   [BL] FOUR MOBILE MAJORS — from the re-run typography + desktop-leak lenses
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   All four confirmed by an adversarial verifier and re-checked against source
   here before writing. Every rule sits inside a max-width query with a ceiling
   of 720px or lower, except the #services token override at 620px — so nothing
   here can reach >=1100px. Deleting this block is a complete revert.

   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1. process #phases — a 91px pill holds 107px of every row hostage

   `.compliance-item` (:459) is `display: flex; align-items: baseline` and
   `.compliance-item__status` (:460) is `flex: 0 0 auto`, so the "Phase 01".."06"
   pill can never leave the copy's line and never shrink. MEASURED at 375: the
   li is 327px (full container) but its copy column is only 220px — 91px pill +
   16px gap = 107px, 29% of the viewport, dead for the full height of each row.
   All six paragraphs run 219-222px = 67-68% of the container.

   Stacking the pill above the copy on mobile returns the whole 327px measure.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
@media (max-width: 700px) {
  .compliance-item {
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--ds-space-xs);
  }
}

/* ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   2. The sticky CTA headline is cut mid-word on 11 pages

   :745 gives `.mm-sticky-cta__copy b` `white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden;
   text-overflow: ellipsis`. MEASURED at 375: clientWidth 158 vs scrollWidth 169
   — 11px over, so the ellipsis fires and the site's most prominent mobile CTA
   reads "Talk to a senior brok…". Width sweep: 320 cuts 66px (14 of 23 chars),
   360 cuts 26px, 375 cuts 11px, and 390 and up cut nothing.

   This is the ONE genuine text truncation on the site, and the site-wide probe
   CANNOT see it — .mm-sticky-cta is on the probe's ESCAPE_OK list (it is fixed
   chrome that legitimately escapes its parent), so the CLIP check never reaches
   it. It was found by reading, not by the gate.

   Placed in the EXISTING @media (max-width: 390px) regime (:835), which already
   hides `.mm-sticky-cta__copy span` — so the bar is showing one line of copy
   there and has room for two. At 391px and up the headline already fits on one
   line, so allowing wrap changes nothing above the query.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
@media (max-width: 390px) {
  .mm-sticky-cta__copy b {
    white-space: normal;
    overflow: visible;
    text-overflow: clip;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }
}

/* ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   3. locations #markets — 40px of measure lost to a UA list indent

   `.loc-types` (:5346) sets display/flex-direction/gap but never `padding: 0`
   or `list-style: none`, so the <ul> keeps the browser default
   `padding-inline-start: 40px`. The sheet is INCONSISTENT with itself about
   this: `.compliance-roadmap__list` at :458 resets both.

   MEASURED box chain at 375: container 375 -> padding 24 -> .loc-tabs 327 ->
   .loc-panel padding 20 -> ul.loc-types 285 with padding-left 40 / right 0 ->
   li.loc-type 245 -> text column 149px. Because the li is display:grid no
   marker ever paints, so the 40px is pure invisible loss, and it is one-sided:
   the rows sit 40px in from the left and flush to the right.

   Added to the existing @media (max-width: 720px) block's regime (:5397).
   Desktop keeps the same indent and is outside the query.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
@media (max-width: 720px) {
  .loc-types { padding-left: 0; list-style: none; }
}

/* ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   4. index #services — seven of eight service names at 11px

   :10547 opens `@media (max-width: 1099px)` with NO min-width floor and sets
   `--md-t-h3-fs: 11px` (:10571) for the master-detail tiles. It is a TABLET
   compression budget applied unchanged down to 320px — the same no-floor
   mechanism as [AR]. Desktop is 14.5px, tablet 12.5px, so 11px is a
   mobile-only value and the smallest type on the site, used as a heading AND a
   tap label.

   MEASURED at 375, this fix A/B'd against two alternatives before choosing:
       CURRENT    min font 11px    section 792px
       13px/62    min font 13px    section 840px   (+48)   <- chosen
       13.5px/66  min font 13.5px  section 856px   (+64)
   No tile clips in any of the three (row scrollHeight == clientHeight at 7/7),
   so the defect here is legibility, not overflow — the lens's claim of a
   clipped tile did NOT reproduce for me and is not repeated as fact.

   Ceiling 620, so the 621-1099 tablet tuning that :10547 was actually written
   for is untouched. A more aggressive single-column mobile layout
   (--md-tile-cols: 1 at 560) was considered and NOT taken: it restructures the
   band, which is an owner-facing design decision rather than a defect fix.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
@media (max-width: 620px) {
  #services .svc-rows.md-on {
    --md-t-h3-fs: 13px;
    --md-tile-h:  62px;
  }
