/* ============================================================================
   [BM] THE REMAINING CONFIRMED MINORS
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Only findings that SURVIVED adversarial verification are here. The following
   were REFUTED by their verifiers and are deliberately NOT acted on, so a later
   reader does not "re-fix" them: the footer's 607px clip (decorative
   pseudo-element, no content hidden) · #services 50x48 thumbnails · the twelve
   512x512 source photographs (an ASSET ceiling, not reachable from CSS at any
   breakpoint) · #disciplines row gap · #about .ab-cluster's dead aspect-ratio ·
   the hero h1's 1.02 line-height · and the two now-inert #industries
   grid-auto-rows clamps at :3684 / :4244 (harmless dead code, left in place).

   All ceilings are 899px or lower. Deleting this block is a complete revert.

   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1. #guides — the TOPIC chip hangs off its own thumbnail

   `--gf-thumb: 76px` is set at :12244 (@media max-width:560px); the chip's
   padding at :12295 was added later and nothing re-checked the fit. MEASURED at
   375 on rows 02 and 03: the chip is 73-74px wide against a 76px thumb and its
   right edge sits 5.2px / 5.5px PAST the photo's right edge, covering 24% of it.

   Two fixes were rendered and measured before choosing:
       CURRENT   overhang +5.5px   chip covers 24%   section 1186px
       thumb 92  overhang -10.5px  chip covers 16%   section 1204px  <- chosen
       chip 9px  overhang -12.9px  chip covers 14%   section 1186px
   The chip-shrink clears more overhang for free, but it takes an already-small
   uppercase label down to 9px. Widening the slot keeps the label at its current
   size AND gives the photograph 21% more area, for 18px of section height.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  #guides { --gf-thumb: 92px; }
}

/* ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   2. #inventory carousel buttons shrink below their declared 44px

   :8617 declares `inline-size: 44px; block-size: 44px`, but the buttons sit in
   `.cov-nav { display: flex }` (:8611) with default `flex-shrink: 1` and
   `min-width: auto`, and the line does not fit at 375 — so they resolve to
   41.2 x 44 and 41.1 x 44. This is the one tap-target defect on the site that
   is a SHRINK bug rather than a missing size: the declared value is already
   correct and is simply not being honoured.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
