/* ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   6. about #disciplines — the 53px photo sliver

   The FOURTH instance of the dead-rule mechanism found this session, and the
   clearest: four same-specificity (0,1,1,0) declarations for
   `#disciplines .cap-showcase__media`, and the LAST one wins at every width.
       :12821  aspect-ratio: 16 / 4     (unscoped)
       :12915  aspect-ratio: 16 / 6     @media (max-width: 899px)   <- the mobile intent
       :12945  aspect-ratio: 16 / 3.4   (unscoped)
       :12966  aspect-ratio: 16 / 2.9   (unscoped)                  <- WINS everywhere
   :12966's own comment shows it came from a DESKTOP viewport-fit exercise
   ("1024 measured WORSE than 1440"). MEASURED at 375: both media boxes render
   293.0 x 53.1 from 512x512 sources — 16/2.9 of a square photograph.

   Re-asserting the author's own @899 value, 16/6, which its verifier measured
   as restoring 293.0 x 109.9 at 375 while leaving 900, 1024, 1100 and 1440
   bit-for-bit identical (at >=1024 the computed aspect-ratio is already `auto`,
   because :13060's min-width block switches the row to a portrait column).
